  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Maa Santoshi Wshg vs State Of Orissa & Others ..... Opposite ... on 14 May, 2024 In The High Court Of Orissa At Cuttack W.P. (C) No.10976 of 2024 Maa Santoshi Wshg, Puri ..... Petitioner Mr. K.P. Mishra, Sr. Advocate Vs. State of Orissa & others ..... Opposite Parties Mr. B. Panigrahi, A.S.C. Coram: Justice Sanjay Kumar Mishra Order 14.05.2024 Order No. 02.",
    "facts": "2. The Petitioner, which is a Women Self Help Group(WSHG), has approached this Court with a prayer for direction to re-engage the Petitioner for preparation and supply of the Take Home Ration (THR) under SNP in respect of Kanas Block in the district of Puri within a stipulated period in view of the report of the Joint Enquiry Team dated 14.08.2023, followed by the recommendation of the Collector, Puri vide Letter No.3119/SW, dated 26.10.2023, addressed to The Director, ICDS & SW Women & Child Development Deptt., Odisha, as at Annexure-3. 3. On perusal of the record, it is ascertained that pursuant to order dated 06.01.2023 passed by the coordinate Bench in W.P.(C) No.29969 of 2020, a District Level Committee was constituted consisting of Deputy Collector, Gen & Misc. Section, Collectorate, Puri, Food Safety Officer, MOCHC, Kanas & DSWO, Puri, who enquired into the matter and submitted a satisfactory report in favour of the Petitioner SHG, there by suggesting to allow the said WSHG for preparation and supply of THR(Chhatua) and based on the said report, the Collector, Puri also communicated to the Director, ICDS & SW, Women & Child Development Deptt., Odisha vide letter dated 26.10.2023(present Opposite Party No.3)",
    "arguments": "4. In response to said submission made by Mr. Mishra, learned Senior Counsel for the Appellant, Mr. B. Panigrahi, learned Additional Standing Counsel for the State, drawing attention of this Court to the report submitted by the Joint Enquiry Team as at Annexure-2 submits, such recommendation was made by the Joint Enquiry Team directing the present Petitioner to submit photocopy of the Food License to DSWO, Puri at an early date and no such averments have been made in the Writ Maa Santoshi Wshg vs State Of Orissa & Others ..... In response to the submissions made by the learned State Counsel, Mr. Mishra, learned Senior Counsel for the Petitioner submits, as per the instruction received from his client, the Petitioner-SHG has already submitted the photocopy of the Food License to DSWO, Puri."
  },
